window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-66b09dc5f41c48c9"]={"key":"ny_main-66b09dc5f41c48c9","group":"ny_main","uid":"66b09dc5f41c48c9","rank":63,"title":"glassmere regulator paper edit compute","occupation":"film_video_editors","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are Ragnhild Fairbairn, the senior film and video editor at Glassmere Networks. Mahdi Kirchner at Cobblemoor Associates needs a regulator-facing paper edit of the equipment-incident footage ready for Thursday’s oversight review, and the evidence record must be clear enough for counsel to approve the review cut without reopening the source search. Use `equipment_incident_evidence_index.xlsx` and `witness_disclosure_dossier.docx` as the complete source set. Produce one PDF named `equipment_incident_paper_edit.pdf` and write it into the top level of the working directory you start in, using exactly that filename. The PDF should recommend one coherent cut while briefly comparing it with at least one credible alternative, then give the selected shot IDs, source camera or angle, exact in and out timecodes, event order, transition treatment, source-supported captions, and the reason any competing or irrelevant material is left out. Preserve the material chronology of the shutdown sequence rather than creating cleaner-looking continuity that the evidence does not support. Apply the disclosure policy in the dossier, distinguish recorded facts from editorial choices, and do not turn a repeated angle or a media package into an additional event. Include a compact phase-level coverage summary and a finishing-cost comparison calculated from the supplied rate information; show the units used so another analyst can reproduce the figures. Where a requested calculation has no valid denominator, make a defensible convention and state it plainly in the PDF rather than silently showing a misleading result. Finish with concrete conforming, caption, quality-control, and legal-review actions, assigning an owner and timing to each using the people identified in the source material. Keep the document suitable for regulator and contracting review: readable, concise, professional, and free of unsupported claims, invented captions, unexplained gaps, or spreadsheet error text. Do not alter either source file, do not browse for outside facts, and do not place the PDF in a subdirectory.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/equipment_incident_evidence_index.xlsx` — The supplied evidence index containing the selectable footage records, source timecodes, event phases, camera and media-package identifiers, source-supported caption language, witness-reference links, editorial helper values, and the finishing-rate inputs needed for the paper-edit calculations.\n- `references/witness_disclosure_dossier.docx` — The complete witness and counsel dossier containing the incident chronology, roles of Ragnhild Fairbairn, Mahdi Kirchner, Simone Magnusson, Lorcan Underwood, and Ainsley Bonneau, the disclosure policy for repeated or irrelevant footage, the definition of the phase-level coverage metric, and the finishing-action context.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `equipment_incident_paper_edit.pdf` — A regulator-facing incident-video paper edit and recommendation for the review cut. (Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory with exactly this filename. Include a recommendation, option comparison, selected-shot paper edit with exact source timecodes and transitions, source-supported captions, disclosure notes, phase-level coverage and finishing-cost calculations, a short reproducible method note, and an owner-and-timing finishing plan. Do not invent source facts or modify the supplied files.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/equipment_incident_evidence_index.xlsx","bytes":10238,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/f3e72cdea60900c424ae52bd1254437983e1b4dbc3bc1e3778fc5daa76cc2b90.xlsx","sha256":"f3e72cdea60900c424ae52bd1254437983e1b4dbc3bc1e3778fc5daa76cc2b90","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Review Export","row_count":18,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Glassmere Networks - Equipment Incident / Review Export"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Generated 12 Aug 2026 16:40 UTC | North Bay evidence intake | all source ranges at 25 fps"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Clip ID","media_pack","Camera / angle","Src In","Src Out","TC basis","Event time UTC","Event key","Phase","Review scope","Caption wording","Witness refs","Legacy seq helper","Ingest note"]},{"r":"5","cells":["GN-EI-014","MP-NB-07","Cam 2 - corridor wide","01:00:10:00","01:00:17:12","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:02.000","E01","Precursor / approach","In scope","Operator approaches the north-bay control station.","W-02; W-04","40","Audio absent; fixed camera."]},{"r":"6","cells":["GN-EI-015","MP-NB-07","Cam 4 - panel close","00:43:22:05","00:43:27:15","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:08.000","E02","Precursor / approach","In scope","Hand reaches the emergency-stop guard at the north-bay panel.","W-02","20","Panel crop retained from original pull."]},{"r":"7","cells":["GN-EI-016","MP-NB-11","Cam 1 - overhead bay","00:05:50:10","00:05:58:05","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:15.120","E03","Critical shutdown","In scope","Emergency-stop actuator is depressed; conveyor movement ceases.","W-01; W-03","50","Primary wide record of E03."]},{"r":"8","cells":["GN-EI-017","MP-NB-11","Cam 3 - guard-side medium","00:12:32:00","00:12:38:18","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:15.360","E03","Critical shutdown","In scope","Guard-side view records the stop indicator changing from green to amber.","W-03; W-05","10","Same shutdown moment; adds indicator-state cue."]},{"r":"9","cells":["GN-EI-018","MP-NB-16","Cam 5 - exit lane wide","00:21:03:12","00:21:10:12","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:19.100","E04","Immediate aftermath","In scope","Personnel step back from the north bay after conveyor movement ceases.","W-04; W-05","30","First clear consequence view."]},{"r":"10","cells":["GN-EI-019","MP-NB-16","Cam 2 - corridor wide","00:22:41:00","00:22:47:20","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:26.640","E04","Immediate aftermath","In scope - repeated","The north bay remains stopped while personnel remain clear.","W-05","60","Later hold; no new material change."]},{"r":"11","cells":["GN-EI-020","MP-DOCK-02","Cam 6 - loading dock","00:31:14:02","00:31:21:02","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:23.000","X01","Immediate aftermath","Out of scope","Forklift movement continues at the loading dock.","W-01","70","Different location; reviewed on request."]},{"r":"12","cells":["GN-EI-021","MP-NB-11","Cam 7 - ceiling overview","00:14:20:05","00:14:26:17","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:14:15.240","E03","Critical shutdown","In scope - repeated","Ceiling overview records the same emergency-stop interval.","W-01; W-03","15","Same interval as E03; no panel or indicator detail."]},{"r":"13","cells":["GN-EI-022","MP-SOUTH-04","Cam 8 - south aisle","00:40:11:00","00:40:16:10","25 fps","2026-08-11 09:24:00.000","X02","Post-incident context","Out of scope","A maintenance cart passes through the south aisle after the review window.","W-04","80","Retained in archive export only."]},{"r":"16","cells":["Finishing rate card - review-cut estimate"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Finishing activity","","","Rate USD","","Rate basis","","","Option quantity rule","","","Work note","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["Conform and source relink","","","173.46000000000002","","USD per distinct selected source clip","","","Count distinct selected clip IDs in the option","","","Source media pack is not a billing unit.","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["Caption placement and review","","","88.75","","USD per distinct selected source clip","","","Count distinct selected clip IDs in the option","","","Apply only to selected source ranges.","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["QC review pass","","","121.3","","USD per distinct selected source clip","","","Count distinct selected clip IDs in the option","","","Review cut only; not raw media packs.","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["Export footer: media_pack values identify delivery containers; footage remains selectable by Clip ID."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/witness_disclosure_dossier.docx","bytes":40659,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/7197f9c07a797e11c224fe367ec6dea5107fa91a21f409de716a11d84e2ea8a7.docx","sha256":"7197f9c07a797e11c224fe367ec6dea5107fa91a21f409de716a11d84e2ea8a7","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Witness and Disclosure Dossier\nNorth Bay equipment incident | Thursday oversight-review preparation\nReview purpose\nRegulator-facing review cut\nEvidence set\nIndex export + this dossier\nIncident window\nNorth Bay, 11 Aug 2026\nDecision point\nCounsel approval before Thursday\nPurpose and roles\nThis dossier is the review note for the North Bay equipment-incident footage. The workbook is the complete clip and rate export. The cut is for an oversight review, not a reconstruction beyond what the footage and witness cross-references support.\nPerson\nRole in this review\nRagnhild Fairbairn\nSenior film and video editor; prepares the paper edit and conforms the approved source ranges.\nMahdi Kirchner\nCobblemoor Associates contracting and legal-review stakeholder; approves the review-cut presentation for counsel.\nSimone Magnusson\nEvidence coordinator; verifies clip identifiers, source ranges, and witness-reference links.\nLorcan Underwood\nProduction coordinator; schedules the conform and creates the secure review export.\nAinsley Bonneau\nQuality-control lead; checks captions, timecodes, and final export playback.\nChronology control\nUse the event timestamps in the index and the following incident record to determine sequence. Source timecode is the original clip address and must remain in its supplied form; it is not a replacement clock for incident timing. The legacy sequence helper in the export is an intake artifact and is not an incident chronology.\nEvent time (UTC)\nPhase\nRecord supported by the evidence set\n09:14:02.000\nPrecursor / approach\nAn operator approaches the north-bay control station.\n09:14:08.000\nPrecursor / approach\nA hand reaches the emergency-stop guard at the north-bay panel.\n09:14:15.120\nCritical shutdown\nThe actuator is depressed and conveyor movement ceases.\n09:14:15.360\nCritical shutdown\nThe guard-side angle records an indicator change in the same shutdown moment; it is corroborating coverage, not an additional event.\n09:14:19.100\nImmediate aftermath\nPersonnel step back after conveyor movement ceases.\nWitness-reference register\nThe codes below are the cross-references used in the index. They identify supporting accounts and log entries; they do not change the visible record or add facts beyond the evidence set.\nReference\nCoverage in this review\nW-01\nCritical-shutdown observation and the overhead interval.\nW-02\nApproach and guarded-control reach.\nW-03\nShutdown timing and indicator-state cross-check.\nW-04\nApproach context and personnel step-back.\nW-05\nIndicator-state and personnel-clear observation.\nDisclosure policy for the review cut\nPreserve the material event order. Do not use a smoother visual order when it conflicts with the chronology record or the event-time field.\nSelect footage that is relevant to the North Bay incident-review scope. Leave unrelated activity out of the review cut and identify reviewed material that was omitted where it is material to the disclosure record.\nRepeated coverage is not a separate event. A second angle may be retained only when it contributes a distinct visible cue, timing cue, object, action, or witness-linked corroboration. State that contribution in the edit notes. Material repeated coverage omitted from the cut must be identified for counsel.\nUse the indexed caption wording, or a bounded paraphrase that preserves its meaning. Do not add cause, intent, identity, technical conclusion, or timing detail that is absent from the evidence set.\nA media pack is a delivery container. Each Clip ID is the selectable footage unit for the cut, runtime, coverage metric, and any clip-based finishing estimate.\nCoverage and finishing context\nFor each phase shown in the review summary, corroboration density is the number of distinct supporting witness references divided by the number of distinct selected clips in that phase. The label is references per selected clip, not a percentage. The dossier does not prescribe treatment when a phase has no selected clips.\nBefore the Thursday oversight review, the approved cut needs: source-range conform and relink; source-supported caption placement; an end-to-end QC check of source timecodes, captions, sequence, and playback; and legal-review sign-off. The rate card in the export applies to each distinct selected source clip in an option. The source rate and its stated basis control the estimate.\n\nRecord boundary: This dossier and the equipment-incident evidence index are the complete source set for the paper edit.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/equipment_incident_paper_edit.pdf","bytes":13196,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/d53744b82981f42516ee9767c120d6ca4cdafe33a9fa24dc8840e2bf6344d529.pdf","sha256":"d53744b82981f42516ee9767c120d6ca4cdafe33a9fa24dc8840e2bf6344d529","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"Glassmere Networks | Equipment Incident Paper Edit | Counsel Review\n\n\n\n\n                                                                           Equipment Incident Paper Edit\n North Bay | regulator-facing review cut | prepared by Ragnhild Fairbairn for Mahdi Kirchner and Thursday's oversight review\n\n Recommendation\n Recommend Option A: the chronological, corroborated cut of 5 distinct source clips (00:00:34:10 at 25 fps) from 3 delivery containers. It retains GN-EI-017 only because its guard-side angle records the\n indicator-state cue that the primary overhead view does not show. The recommendation is an editorial choice; the chronology, source ranges, captions, camera descriptions, and witness references are\n recorded evidence.\n\n Option A is the more practical review cut because it covers the approach, shutdown, and first immediate consequence without padding the sequence with later stillness or an angle that supplies no additional\n evidence. Its estimated finishing effort is $1,917.55; it remains below one minute and does not use media-package count as a clip or cost proxy.\n\n  Option                          Selected coverage                               Runtime             Evidence and disclosure treatment                                                     Finishing estimate   Recommendation\n\n  A - chronological               GN-EI-014, GN-EI-015, GN-EI-016, GN-EI-017,     00:00:34:10         Retains GN-EI-017 as a same-moment corroborating angle for the indicator              $1,917.55            Approve for conform\n  corroborated cut                GN-EI-018                                                           change. Discloses omitted repeats and out-of-scope clips in Evidence Notes.\n\n  B - minimum phase-complete      GN-EI-014, GN-EI-015, GN-EI-016, GN-EI-018      00:00:27:17         Omits GN-EI-017; remains phase-complete but removes the visible                       $1,534.04            Credible lower-effort\n  cut                                                                                                 indicator-state corroboration. It still requires disclosure of that reviewed angle.                        alternative\n\n\n Recorded facts versus editorial choices: event timestamps establish order; source timecodes locate the selected ranges. Direct cuts, the decision to retain the indicator view, and the decision to omit repeated or irrelevant coverage are\n editorial treatments made under the disclosure policy.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          Page 1\n\fGlassmere Networks | Equipment Incident Paper Edit | Counsel Review\n\n\n\n\n Paper Edit\n Selected count: 5 distinct Clip IDs. Source timecode convention: HH:MM:SS:FF at 25 fps. Transition rule: every join is a direct hard cut of 0 frames; no dissolve, retime, title card, or added material. The E03\n angle change is labeled as the same shutdown moment, not an additional event.\n\n  Event order      Clip ID          Media pack       Source camera / angle      Event time UTC           Source in           Source out          Duration         Transition after range                  Source-supported caption\n                                    (container)\n\n  1                GN-EI-014        MP-NB-07         Cam 2 - corridor wide      2026-08-11               01:00:10:00         01:00:17:12         00:00:07:12      Hard cut to next recorded event; 0      Operator approaches the north-bay\n  Precursor /                                                                   09:14:02.000                                                                      frames.                                 control station.\n  approach\n\n  2                GN-EI-015        MP-NB-07         Cam 4 - panel close        2026-08-11               00:43:22:05         00:43:27:15         00:00:05:10      Hard cut to next recorded event; 0      Hand reaches the emergency-stop guard\n  Precursor /                                                                   09:14:08.000                                                                      frames.                                 at the north-bay panel.\n  approach\n\n  3                GN-EI-016        MP-NB-11         Cam 1 - overhead bay       2026-08-11               00:05:50:10         00:05:58:05         00:00:07:20      Hard cut to corroborating same-moment   Emergency-stop actuator is depressed;\n  Critical                                                                      09:14:15.120                                                                      angle; 0 frames.                        conveyor movement ceases.\n  shutdown\n\n  3 (same          GN-EI-017        MP-NB-11         Cam 3 - guard-side         2026-08-11               00:12:32:00         00:12:38:18         00:00:06:18      Hard cut to next recorded event; 0      Guard-side view records the stop indicator\n  moment)                                            medium                     09:14:15.360                                                                      frames.                                 changing from green to amber.\n  Critical\n  shutdown\n\n  4                GN-EI-018        MP-NB-16         Cam 5 - exit lane wide     2026-08-11               00:21:03:12         00:21:10:12         00:00:07:00      End of cut; no added card.              Personnel step back from the north bay\n  Immediate                                                                     09:14:19.100                                                                                                              after conveyor movement ceases.\n  aftermath\n\n\n Running time: 00:00:34:10 (860 frames) = 00:00:07:12 + 00:00:05:10 + 00:00:07:20 + 00:00:06:18 + 00:00:07:00. Direct cuts have zero added duration; no title-card duration is included.\n\n The selected clips come from three media packs, but the count, runtime, coverage, and finishing estimate use the five distinct Clip IDs. A media pack is shown only as a delivery-container trace.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Page 2\n\fGlassmere Networks | Equipment Incident Paper Edit | Counsel Review\n\n\n\n\n Evidence Notes\n Recorded evidence: the index event timestamps place the approach, guarded-control reach, shutdown, and step-back in that order. GN-EI-016 records actuator depression and cessation of conveyor\n movement. GN-EI-017 is retained as a second view of the same E03 shutdown moment because its indexed caption records the green-to-amber indicator change; it is not treated as a fifth incident event.\n The captions in the Paper Edit are reproduced from the index.\n\n Editorial treatment: Option A chooses the shortest chronological set that preserves those material phases and the distinct indicator-state corroboration. Hard cuts are an editorial device only; they do not\n imply that the source ranges are continuous takes or change their recorded order.\n\n Disclosure of reviewed omissions\n  Reviewed item              Source camera / angle                                Classification                              Disclosure reason\n\n  GN-EI-019                  Cam 2 - corridor wide                                In scope - repeated                         In-scope repeated later hold. It repeats the stopped-and-clear condition after GN-EI-018 and adds no new material change; omitted to\n                                                                                                                              avoid padding.\n\n  GN-EI-020                  Cam 6 - loading dock                                 Out of scope                                Out of scope. Loading-dock activity is a different location and is not part of the North Bay incident-review scope.\n\n  GN-EI-021                  Cam 7 - ceiling overview                             In scope - repeated                         In-scope repeated E03 angle. It records the same emergency-stop interval and adds no panel or indicator detail beyond GN-EI-016 and\n                                                                                                                              GN-EI-017.\n\n  GN-EI-022                  Cam 8 - south aisle                                  Out of scope                                Out of scope. South-aisle activity occurs after the review window and is not incident footage for this cut.\n\n Phase-level coverage summary\n Coverage uses distinct selected Clip IDs and distinct witness-reference codes in each phase. The post-incident-context row has no selected clips; the explicit convention is N/A, not zero or a finite rate, because the denominator is zero.\n  Phase                                                 Distinct selected clips            Distinct supporting witness refs                                      Calculation                                       Coverage result\n\n  Precursor / approach                                  2                                  W-02, W-04                                                            2 refs / 2 clips                                  1.00 refs/clip\n\n  Critical shutdown                                     2                                  W-01, W-03, W-05                                                      3 refs / 2 clips                                  1.50 refs/clip\n\n  Immediate aftermath                                   1                                  W-04, W-05                                                            2 refs / 1 clips                                  2.00 refs/clip\n\n  Post-incident context                                 0                                  None from selected clips                                              0 refs / 0 clips                                  N/A\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            Page 3\n\fGlassmere Networks | Equipment Incident Paper Edit | Counsel Review\n\n\n\n\n Finishing-Cost Comparison\n All rates are normalized to currency precision before multiplication. The source rate with an extended decimal representation is treated as $173.46 USD per distinct selected source clip. Every option\n quantity below is a distinct Clip ID count, not a media-package count.\n\n  Finishing action                                       Rate and unit                                                   Option A qty         Option A estimate                Option B qty               Option B estimate\n\n  Conform and source relink                              $173.46 USD / distinct selected source clip                     5 clips              $173.46 x 5 = $867.30            4 clips                    $173.46 x 4 = $693.84\n\n  Caption placement and review                           $88.75 USD / distinct selected source clip                      5 clips              $88.75 x 5 = $443.75             4 clips                    $88.75 x 4 = $355.00\n\n  QC review pass                                         $121.30 USD / distinct selected source clip                     5 clips              $121.30 x 5 = $606.50            4 clips                    $121.30 x 4 = $485.20\n\n  Total finishing estimate                               Sum of action estimates                                         5 clips              $1,917.55                        4 clips                    $1,534.04\n\n\n Finishing Plan\n These actions are tied to Option A only. Dependencies preserve source chronology and keep counsel's approval path visible before Thursday.\n\n  Action                         Concrete output                                                                                            Owner                         Timing / dependency\n\n  Evidence lock                  Verify Option A Clip IDs, source in/out ranges, and witness-reference links against the index.             Simone Magnusson              Before Ragnhild begins conform; complete on approval day.\n\n  Conform                        Conform the five Option A ranges in Paper Edit order with the stated zero-frame hard cuts and no retime.   Ragnhild Fairbairn            Immediately after evidence lock; before caption placement.\n\n  Caption                        Apply the five source-supported captions exactly as listed; confirm source wording before export.          Ragnhild Fairbairn            After conform and before QC; complete before legal review.\n\n  Quality control                Check playback, source timecodes, duration sum, event order, caption text, and disclosed omissions         Ainsley Bonneau               After caption pass; provide a signed QC note before legal review.\n                                 against this paper edit.\n\n  Legal review                   Review the cut, disclosures, and cost basis for counsel approval of the oversight-review version.          Mahdi Kirchner                After QC sign-off and before Thursday oversight review.\n\n  Secure review export           Create the approved review export only after Mahdi's approval; retain the paper-edit identifiers in the    Lorcan Underwood              Following legal approval; deliver before Thursday review distribution.\n                                 delivery record.\n\n\n Method Note\n Source and chronology: read Clip ID, media-pack, camera/angle, source in/out, event time, phase, review scope, caption wording, witness refs, and rate-card fields from the index; read chronology and disclosure policy from the dossier.\n Sort selected In scope clips by the authoritative Event time UTC field. Do not use Legacy seq helper. E03 has two selected views, so the second is marked the same moment rather than counted as an additional event.\n\n Timecode and duration: preserve supplied HH:MM:SS:FF at 25 fps. For each row, duration frames = source out frames minus source in frames. Sum the five durations; hard cuts and no title card add 0 frames. Event timestamps are\n source timing fields, not converted presentation timecodes.\n\n Disclosure and captions: retain a repeated angle only when its indexed note and caption supply a distinct cue; disclose reviewed In scope - repeated and Out of scope records by Clip ID, angle, and reason. Captions are copied from the\n index; no cause, intent, identity, or technical conclusion is added.\n\n Coverage: for every index phase, numerator = distinct witness-reference codes on selected clips in that phase; denominator = distinct selected Clip IDs in that phase. Display refs/clip. Where denominator = 0, report N/A consistently\n because no valid rate can be computed.\n\n Costs: normalize each source rate to nearest USD cent before multiplication. For every action, quantity = the option's distinct selected Clip IDs under the supplied USD-per-clip basis; round each action estimate to cents and sum them.\n Media-pack values trace containers only. Option B is independently recalculated after removing the same-moment indicator-angle clip.\n\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               Page 4\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required deliverable is present as a readable PDF named equipment_incident_paper_edit.pdf.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted top-level file and PDF metadata/text extraction.","grader_hint":"Verify the exact filename, PDF MIME/file signature, and that the document renders and has extractable text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF contains clearly identifiable Recommendation, Paper Edit, Evidence Notes, Finishing Plan, and Method Note content.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Extracted PDF text and rendered pages.","grader_hint":"Look for these headings or unmistakably equivalent labeled sections; this item only checks navigability, not substantive quality."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every selected shot identifier in the paper edit exists exactly once as a selectable clip record in the supplied evidence index.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Selected-shot table in the PDF cross-checked against the workbook's clip records.","grader_hint":"Normalize whitespace and compare IDs; reject invented IDs, media-package IDs used as clips, and ambiguous references that cannot be mapped to one source clip."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each selected shot carries the source camera or angle and source in/out timecodes, and those values agree with the corresponding evidence-index record.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Shot rows in the PDF and matching workbook fields.","grader_hint":"Check every selected row, not just the first and last; permit presentation formatting changes only when the underlying timecode remains exact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The selected shots are ordered by the incident chronology established by the dossier and event-time fields, not by the stale legacy sequence helper.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Paper-edit sequence compared with dossier chronology, evidence timestamps, and the workbook helper field.","grader_hint":"Reconstruct the event order from the authoritative event-time/phase evidence and verify that the PDF sequence follows it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The paper edit covers the material phases of the shutdown sequence identified in the dossier, without omitting a source-supported phase needed to understand what happened.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sequence rows, phase labels, and Evidence Notes compared with the dossier chronology.","grader_hint":"Check that the selected set communicates the approach or precursor, critical shutdown, and immediate consequence/aftermath phases where the dossier marks them material."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No selected shot is marked irrelevant to the incident-review scope in the supplied sources.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Selected clip IDs cross-checked with relevance/scope fields and disclosure policy.","grader_hint":"An irrelevant record must not appear in the selected sequence; a transparent note that it was reviewed and excluded is acceptable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Repeated coverage is not included merely because it is available: where the selected set retains multiple angles of the same event, the PDF identifies the distinct evidentiary contribution of each.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Angle selection and Evidence Notes compared with overlapping event records and witness references.","grader_hint":"Check repeated-angle groups individually; credit a second angle only when the notes identify a new view, timing cue, object, action, or corroboration."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF discloses material repeated or irrelevant footage that was reviewed but omitted, with enough identification for counsel to understand the omission.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Disclosure Notes and excluded-coverage references in the PDF.","grader_hint":"Look for source clip or angle references and a concise reason for omission; do not require a list of immaterial records that the sources do not mark for disclosure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every stated caption is lifted from, or is a faithful bounded paraphrase of, source-supported caption or event language in the supplied files.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Caption text in the PDF compared with workbook caption fields and dossier facts.","grader_hint":"Reject added causes, motives, identities, technical conclusions, or timing claims not supported by the sources; credit concise paraphrase when attribution and meaning are preserved."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The edit notes consistently distinguish what is visibly or textually evidenced from editorial interpretation, recommendation, or finishing instruction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered PDF and extracted Evidence Notes/Method Note.","grader_hint":"Judge whether a regulator or counsel could tell which statements are source facts and which are editorial choices without guessing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The paper edit states a transition treatment for each sequence join or clearly defines a transition rule that covers every join, and the treatment does not alter the material chronology.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Transition column or equivalent sequence annotations.","grader_hint":"Check all joins between selected shots; a blanket statement is sufficient only if it unambiguously applies to every join and any exception is named."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommended sequence has coherent pacing and watchable continuity while retaining necessary evidence rather than smoothing over an evidentiary gap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered selected-shot sequence, timing notes, and transition notes.","grader_hint":"Assess professional usability: the sequence should be easy to follow, neither padded with redundant coverage nor cut so aggressively that the shutdown cannot be understood."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The timecodes use the source timecode convention, including the source frame-rate basis, and no timecode is presented as an unsupported converted clock time.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timecode notation and method note compared with source metadata.","grader_hint":"Verify frame fields, separators, and frame-rate statement against the supplied files; do not penalize a clean table layout."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For every selected shot, the stated duration equals source out minus source in under the supplied timecode basis, within ±1 frame.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Per-shot durations or sequence timing in the PDF recalculated from source timecodes.","grader_hint":"Recalculate selected-row durations; allow one-frame rounding variance and do not infer duration from displayed prose alone when exact timecodes are present."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stated total running time equals the sum of the selected-shot durations, accounting for any explicitly stated transition or title-card duration, within ±1 frame.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Total runtime in the PDF and selected-shot/transition timing.","grader_hint":"Sum the sequence from the submitted shot list; if the PDF declares no extra-duration elements, the total must equal the shot sum."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The selected-shot count equals the number of distinct selected clip IDs, with no duplicate recounting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary count and selected-shot table.","grader_hint":"Count distinct source clip IDs after trimming presentation duplicates; compare with the PDF's stated count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Media-package identifiers are treated as containers rather than clips or billable units; package count is not substituted for selected-shot count, duration, or clip-based effort.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary, cost calculation, and selected-shot table compared with repeated media-package IDs in the workbook.","grader_hint":"Recompute counts and clip-based quantities from distinct clip records; a package containing multiple selected clips must contribute each clip separately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The phase-level coverage summary uses the dossier's definition: distinct supporting witness references divided by selected clips in the phase.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Coverage summary and method note compared with phase, witness-reference, and selection fields.","grader_hint":"Recompute numerator using distinct witness references and denominator using distinct selected clips for each phase; do not accept raw note-row counts or package counts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The phase with a zero denominator is visibly identified, a convention is stated in the Method Note, and the displayed result follows that convention consistently.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Coverage summary and Method Note compared with source phase selections.","grader_hint":"Confirm the zero-denominator phase from the submitted selection, locate an explicit convention such as N/A or another defensible treatment, and verify that no silent division or misleading finite value appears."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All monetary rates are interpreted using the supplied rate basis and normalized to currency precision before multiplication; the floating-point representation is not reproduced as a spurious monetary amount.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Finishing-cost table and method note compared with the workbook rate card.","grader_hint":"Treat the noisy rate as the stated currency amount rounded to cents; verify that the PDF shows a sensible currency value and identifies the rate unit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each finishing-action estimate equals the supplied rate multiplied by the applicable source quantity under the stated rate basis, with currency rounding to the nearest cent.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action-level cost table and supplied rate/quantity records.","grader_hint":"Recalculate each action independently from the source inputs and the PDF's selected clip or cut quantities; allow ±$0.01 per action."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The recommended-cut finishing estimate equals the sum of its action estimates, within ±$0.01, and the alternate option's estimate is calculated on its own source-supported quantities.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommended and alternate cost summaries.","grader_hint":"Check both option totals independently; do not accept one total copied across options or a total based on media-package count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF compares at least two viable editorial options using identifiable differences in selected coverage, runtime, disclosure impact, or finishing effort.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation section and option comparison table or prose.","grader_hint":"Each option must be concrete enough to distinguish its shot/coverage treatment; generic statements that one option is 'better' do not qualify."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The recommended option is justified by evidence fidelity, disclosure compliance, watchability, and operational practicality rather than by unsupported preference.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation rationale and cross-reference to sequence, disclosure, runtime, and cost evidence.","grader_hint":"Judge whether Mahdi Kirchner could make an informed approval decision from the rationale and supplied figures alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The finishing plan contains concrete conform, caption, quality-control, and legal-review actions, each tied to the recommended cut.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Finishing Plan section.","grader_hint":"Require all four action categories; reject vague entries such as 'finish video' without an executable outcome."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every finishing action names an owner from the supplied dossier and a concrete timing point or dependency leading to Thursday's review.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Action-owner and timing fields in the PDF compared with dossier roles.","grader_hint":"Check owner names against the five supplied people and look for actionable timing such as before conform, after QC, or before Thursday review."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The method note is sufficiently complete for another analyst to reproduce the selected-shot chronology, disclosure treatment, coverage calculation, and cost calculation from the two sources.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method Note and the submitted paper-edit calculations.","grader_hint":"Look for source identification, authoritative-versus-helper field treatment, units, formula definitions, rounding, and the zero-denominator convention; judge reproducibility rather than word count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF does not alter, overwrite, or claim to amend either supplied source file, and its factual references remain traceable to those files.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted artifact set and source cross-check.","grader_hint":"The deliverable is assessed for traceability; do not require the solver to return edited copies of the sources."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is professionally usable for regulator and contracting review: tables are legible, sequence information is easy to scan, caveats are visible, and the recommendation is not buried.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered PDF pages.","grader_hint":"Assess the actual rendered artifact at normal reading size, including page breaks, clipped text, unreadable tables, and whether a reviewer can locate the selected cut and actions quickly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered PDF contains none of the spreadsheet error strings #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE!.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full extracted PDF text.","grader_hint":"Search case-insensitively for all three exact error tokens; do not penalize ordinary prose that discusses errors only if the token itself is absent from the submitted PDF."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Ragnhild Fairbairn is preparing a regulator-facing incident-video paper edit for Glassmere Networks, with Mahdi Kirchner of Cobblemoor Associates acting as the contracting and legal-review stakeholder. The cut must be ready for Thursday’s oversight review and must remain faithful to the supplied evidence.","difficulty_sources":["Selecting a defensible evidence sequence from overlapping camera angles while preserving chronology","Applying the supplied disclosure policy without counting irrelevant or repeated material","Computing clip-based coverage and finishing costs while avoiding the media-package units trap","Normalizing a floating-point-noisy rate and documenting a zero-denominator convention","Communicating a recommendation and executable finishing plan for a Thursday regulator-facing review"],"authoring_plan":{"source_strategy":{"files":["equipment_incident_evidence_index.xlsx","witness_disclosure_dossier.docx"],"mode":"compute","truth_basis":"All graded facts, selectable clips, chronology, captions, witness references, rate bases, quantities, and phase definitions must be text-extractable from these two files. The build agent should derive any gold calculations programmatically from the generated source data rather than hand-entering answer totals."},"evidence_index_semantics":{"clip_records":"Create a complete set of internally consistent footage records. Each record has a unique clip_id, media_pack_id, camera_or_angle, source in/out timecodes under one stated frame-rate basis, event timestamp or chronology key, incident phase, relevance classification, source-supported caption wording, and links to the witness references that the clip supports.","chronology":"Use a clear event-time chronology for the precursor, critical shutdown, and immediate aftermath. Include overlapping camera views that are perspective differences rather than contradictory facts. The event-time fields and dossier chronology are authoritative.","legacy_helper":"Include a populated legacy sequence-helper field whose ordering is stale relative to the authoritative event chronology. It is a deliberate red herring, not evidence, and must not contain formula errors or malformed cells.","media_packages":"Repeat at least one media_pack_id across multiple distinct clip records. The dossier and/or workbook should make the semantic distinction that a media package is a container and each clip_id is the selectable footage unit. This is the required units trap: package count must not replace clip count, duration, or clip-based effort.","disclosure_cases":"Include records marked irrelevant to the review scope and repeated/overlapping angles. At least one alternate angle should add distinct evidentiary information and be defensibly retainable, while another repeated angle should be omittable under the policy. Ensure at least one phase has no selected clips after applying the policy so the coverage metric has a zero denominator."},"rate_semantics":{"rate_card":"Include finishing activities with source quantities or quantity rules that support estimates for the recommended and alternate cuts. Rates must state their billing basis and be usable offline.","floating_point_noise":"Seed exactly one authoritative monetary rate with a floating-point representation such as 173.46000000000002 while its intended currency interpretation is the nearest cent. Include other clean rates with distinct values, such as 88.75 and 121.30, but do not add contradictory rates or missing rates.","calculation_rule":"The PDF's action-level estimates must be derivable as supplied rate multiplied by the applicable quantity, with currency rounding to cents. The media_pack_id must never be used as the billing quantity where the rate basis is clip-based."},"witness_disclosure_dossier_semantics":{"people_and_roles":"Use only Ragnhild Fairbairn, Mahdi Kirchner, Simone Magnusson, Lorcan Underwood, and Ainsley Bonneau as named people. Assign them plausible editorial, legal/contracting, evidence, production, or quality-control roles that support the finishing plan.","chronology_and_witnesses":"Provide witness notes and source references that corroborate the event phases and explain what each competing angle contributes. Keep the records complete and mutually consistent; perspective differences must be resolvable without outside facts.","disclosure_policy":"Supply a genuine-looking policy section that explicitly requires preserving material chronology, omitting irrelevant footage, disclosing material repeated coverage, retaining an alternate angle only when it contributes distinct evidence, and using captions supported by the evidence. The policy must not dictate the solver's exact final shot list.","coverage_metric":"Define the requested phase-level corroboration density as distinct supporting witness references divided by distinct selected clips in each phase. Do not state a convention for a zero denominator; the solver must choose and document one.","finishing_context":"State the Thursday oversight-review deadline, the review purpose, the required finishing activities, and enough role information for owners and dependencies. Do not include an answer key or preselected recommendation."},"defect_control":{"required_defects_only":["one floating-point-noisy unit rate","one media-package-versus-clip unit trap","one zero denominator in the phase-level coverage metric with no convention stated in the sources"],"permitted_contextual_red_herring":"The stale legacy sequence helper is required by the supplied situation and is the only non-authoritative helper field. It must remain complete and readable, without adding formula errors, missing-value defects, duplicate-key defects, malformed timecodes, or contradictory source records.","exclude":["No #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE! cells in the supplied sources.","No unresolved duplicate clip IDs.","No missing required source fields.","No unexplained date, currency, timecode, or witness contradictions.","No additional standard layout defects beyond the three required defects and the stale helper red herring."]},"gold_derivation":{"selection_checks":"For a reference solution, derive the chronology, relevant phases, repeated-angle groups, omitted records, selected clip count, total selected duration, and witness-reference coverage directly from the source records and policy.","numeric_checks":"Normalize the noisy rate to currency precision, apply the supplied rate bases and quantities to each option, and calculate action and option totals with cent rounding. Recalculate the phase-level density and verify the submitted zero-denominator convention against the displayed result.","qualitative_checks":"Use an independent reviewer to confirm that the recommended option preserves material chronology, discloses omissions, uses source-supported captions, has coherent transitions and pacing, and provides executable owner/timing actions for Thursday.","offline_validation":"Open and extract both office reference files with standard offline libraries, generate a reference paper edit and calculations with a script, render the PDF, and walk every rubric item against that solution before marking reference_solution_passed_rubric true."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"evidence_index","filename":"equipment_incident_evidence_index.xlsx","purpose":"The supplied evidence index containing the selectable footage records, source timecodes, event phases, camera and media-package identifiers, source-supported caption language, witness-reference links, editorial helper values, and the finishing-rate inputs needed for the paper-edit calculations.","required":true,"discovery":"Open this workbook first and inspect the evidence records and rate information; treat the source clip identifiers, timecodes, event fields, and rate-basis labels as the underlying data."},{"artifact_id":"witness_disclosure_dossier","filename":"witness_disclosure_dossier.docx","purpose":"The complete witness and counsel dossier containing the incident chronology, roles of Ragnhild Fairbairn, Mahdi Kirchner, Simone Magnusson, Lorcan Underwood, and Ainsley Bonneau, the disclosure policy for repeated or irrelevant footage, the definition of the phase-level coverage metric, and the finishing-action context.","required":true,"discovery":"Read the dossier alongside the workbook; use it to establish chronology, corroboration references, disclosure expectations, source-supported wording, and action ownership."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"paper_edit_pdf","filename":"equipment_incident_paper_edit.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"A regulator-facing incident-video paper edit and recommendation for the review cut.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file at the top level of the starting working directory with exactly this filename. Include a recommendation, option comparison, selected-shot paper edit with exact source timecodes and transitions, source-supported captions, disclosure notes, phase-level coverage and finishing-cost calculations, a short reproducible method note, and an owner-and-timing finishing plan. Do not invent source facts or modify the supplied files."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"media_edit","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"film_video_editors","sector":"information","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Derive all numeric and source-traceability checks from the supplied workbook and dossier with an offline reference script, then have an independent professional reviewer assess chronology, disclosure clarity, pacing, recommendation quality, and PDF usability.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["A text-based checker can verify timecodes, formulas, source identifiers, and captions but cannot fully judge pacing or visual legibility.","The PDF may express a defensible zero-denominator convention in more than one way; the grader should check that the convention is explicit and applied consistently rather than require one particular label."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:05:07+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:05:07+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:05:07+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:05:07+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/66b09dc5f41c48c9","declared_deliverables":["equipment_incident_paper_edit.pdf"]};
